{"duration_api_ms":717076,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"82312e0d-84f4-418f-aa4b-0abc53f02c04","total_cost_usd":31.1343445,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11922,"cache_read_input_tokens":2943329,"output_tokens":4510,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1535},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11922,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":494995,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":232,"outputTokens":58240,"thinkingTokens":14652,"cacheReadInputTokens":44974489,"cacheCreationInputTokens":718994,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":31.1343445,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":7,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The redirect path is still reachable for POST, so this is not dead code: D5 changed only the *connection-error* branch (`err.response == null`), while the manual redirect lives in the `err.response != null` 3xx branch, which this interceptor exists precisely to handle for methods dart:io will not follow itself — POST included. So when the redirect leaves the origin, I now also scrub the body: `_scrubBody` removes `access_key`, `mobile_access_key`, `csrf`, `csrf_token`, `biliCSRF` and the signatures over them (`sign`, `w_rid`) from a map body or a `FormData`'s fields, matching the key set `AccountManager` already scrubs for anonymised requests. It runs inside the same cross-origin branch, so same-origin redirects (including 307/308 replays) are untouched, and the 303 path that nulls the body is unaffected; other body types (streams, raw strings/bytes) are left alone.\n\n## Diff\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/lib/http/retry_interceptor.dart b/lib/http/retry_interceptor.dart\n@@\n                 ..extra['account'] = const NoAccount();\n+              // 307/308 (and a POST this interceptor follows itself) keep\n+              // the body: take the account's secrets out of it too\n+              _scrubBody(options);\n             }\n             (options..path = redirectUrl).maxRedirects--;\n@@\n+  /// Account secrets a body may carry (see AccountManager) and the\n+  /// signatures computed over them: worthless at another origin, and the\n+  /// account's to keep.\n+  static const _bodySecrets = [\n+    'access_key',\n+    'mobile_access_key',\n+    'csrf',\n+    'csrf_token',\n+    'biliCSRF',\n+    'sign',\n+    'w_rid',\n+  ];\n+\n+  static void _scrubBody(RequestOptions options) {\n+    switch (options.data) {\n+      case final Map data:\n+        data.removeWhere((key, _) => _bodySecrets.contains(key));\n+      case final FormData data:\n+        data.fields.removeWhere((e) => _bodySecrets.contains(e.key));\n+    }\n+  }\n+\n   RetryInterceptor copyWith({Dio? client, int? count, int? delay}) =>\n```\n\n(The other hunks `git diff` shows in this file are the earlier A11 and D5 changes, unchanged here.)\n\nOne thing I did not verify: the map body is mutated in place, like `AccountManager._scrubAccessKey` does, so a caller passing a `const` map to a request that then gets a cross-origin redirect would throw. Every body in this codebase is a plain map literal, so I left it consistent with the existing scrub rather than copying the map.\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (preceded by dart analyze lib test)\n  command: source local_env.sh && cd C:/Users/Z14/Documents/Coding/Piliplus && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 102\n  passed: 102\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~297000 (analyze ~280s, test ~17s)\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```","ttft_ms":4656,"type":"result","duration_ms":183913,"uuid":"7545f45e-fa00-4bfe-85da-335c80e9e6e1","ttft_stream_ms":3350,"time_to_request_ms":504,"first_content_frame_ms":3351,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
